SYSTEM OVERVIEW
===============
The Role-based Access Control (RBAC) system is designed to manage permissions and roles across multiple users in a secure manner. It supports role hierarchy, temporary role delegation, revocation of delegated roles, and concurrent request processing. The system is built to ensure authorization correctness, consistency in delegation and permissions, and safe, live processing of requests under concurrency. The system includes a security clearance model with levels: High, Medium, and Low. A new Emergency Module is being integrated into this system to handle emergency situations with specific protocols.

PROSPECTIVE COMPONENT REQUIREMENTS
=======================
R1: Emergency Trigger
While operating in Normal mode, exactly 2 administrators are required to trigger an emergency, causing the system to enter the Emergency mode.

R2: Emergency Duration
The Emergency mode is active for a fixed duration, but it has the option to be terminated early if both administrators deactivate the Emergency mode.

R3: Emergency Mode Operations
During the Emergency mode:
    R3.1. Request processing may bypass the FIFO order to prioritize processing multiple high classification requests concurrently, followed by medium, and then low classification requests.
    R3.2. Users may temporarily hold mutually exclusive roles.
    R3.3. Administrators temporarily hold emergency privileges.

R4: Post-Emergency Restoration
After Emergency mode ends:
    R4.1. Emergency privileges must be revoked.
    R4.2. Delegated roles during the emergency must be revoked.
    R4.3. Administrators must update their credentials.

KEY CONCEPTS AND ENTITIES
==========================
- User: An individual in the system with a security clearance.
- Administrator: A user with a High security clearance and administrative privileges.
- Role: A set of permissions that can be assigned or delegated to users.
- Request: An action submitted by a user to affect one or more system objects.
- Emergency Mode: A system state triggered by administrators for handling emergencies.
- FIFO Order: First-In-First-Out processing order for requests.

ASSUMPTIONS REQUIRING CLARIFICATION
====================================
1. [None - All previous assumptions have been clarified.]

CONSTRAINTS
===========
- The system must ensure that only users with appropriate clearance levels can submit or approve requests.
- Emergency mode must be triggered by exactly two administrators.
- Emergency mode must eventually end, reverting the system to Normal mode.
- Role delegations during Emergency mode must be revocable upon its conclusion.
```

